T*
() Tj
T*
(INTERPRETATION) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Evaluation 2 is better than Evaluation 1 in one important sense: it measures the system on a ) Tj
T*
(question set that is more aligned with the intended retrieval scope. That makes the result easier to) Tj
T*
( trust as a signal about the current code-and-doc RAG pipeline rather than as a mixture of code ) Tj
T*
(retrieval quality and off-scope example coverage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(At the same time, the comparison also shows that simply filtering the question set was not enough. ) Tj
T*
(The remaining weak areas are exactly the ones we investigated during development: precise ) Tj
T*
(implementation-location questions, algorithm questions that need the right solver file instead of a ) Tj
T*
(nearby helper, and data-flow questions that need evidence from more than one subsystem.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The strongest improvement in process quality is not a single score jump; it is that the work between) Tj
T*
( the two runs made the benchmark more focused and made retrieval behavior more explicit and ) Tj
T*
(controllable. That gives a much better foundation for the next round of iteration.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(CONCLUSION) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In short: Evaluation 2 is a cleaner benchmark, a slightly stronger result numerically, and a much ) Tj
T*
(better reflection of the retrieval work we actually did. The main development themes between the ) Tj
T*
(runs were narrowing the benchmark to src/ plus docs, improving exact location retrieval, improving ) Tj
T*
(solver comparison retrieval, and reducing prompt noise from supplementary chunks.) Tj
T*
ET
